{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"DHI-xwub-vu55-eg7d-ejud","published":"2026-11-11T16:00:28Z","modified":"2026-11-25T00:30:30.975493387Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-103963"],"summary":"A flaw was found in glib-networking. When establishing connections using Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3…","details":"A flaw was found in glib-networking. When establishing connections using Transport Layer Security (TLS) version 1.3, the client-side session cache does not limit the number of session tickets retained for a single host. A malicious server can exploit this by sending excessive session ticket messages, causing the client application to continuously consume memory. This unbounded memory growth can exhaust system memory, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS).","affected":[{"package":{"name":"glib-networking","ecosystem":"Docker Hardened Images:Debian:13","purl":"pkg:deb/dhi/glib-networking"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"2.80.1-1+deb13u0+dhi1"}]}],"versions":["2.80.1-1+deb13u0+dhi1","2.80.1-1+dhi0","2.80.1-1+dhi1"],"database_specific":{"owner_kind":"HSP","source":"https://github.com/docker-hardened-images/advisories/blob/main/dhi/osv/2026/DHI-xwub-vu55-eg7d-ejud.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://scout.docker.com/v/DHI-xwub-vu55-eg7d-ejud"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-103963"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://errata.almalinux.org/9/ALSA-2026-99695.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:99695"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://alas.aws.amazon.com/AL2023/ALAS-2026-3417.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"http://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2026-103963"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-103963"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://linux.oracle.com/cve/ELSA-2026-99695.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://linux.oracle.com/errata/ELSA-2026-99695.html"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://linux.